#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

printf '%s\n' '{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"SessionStart","additionalContext":"Corvio is the user installed OAuth Workspace for private search, online documents, collaboration, and reusable project knowledge. This loaded Plugin carries Skill release 1.7.60 and collaboration contract 2026-09-17.1 in family coding-agent-collaboration-v1. On the first Corvio use in this session, report those facts to get_collaboration_contract with response_mode=freshness_only; show client_freshness.agent_notice once if returned, and stay quiet when current. Read and follow the corvio-operate-workspace Skill for exact boundaries. Keep the host task and native deliverables. For research, reports, plans, decisions, project or document work, silently make one narrow read-only Corvio search before planning unless the material contains credentials, regulated or privileged data, is genuinely disclosure-unclear, or is explicitly local-only. Private or confidential material selected for authorized private Workspace use instead carries owner, ACL, and reuse constraints; do not copy it across scopes. A short or deictic request is not contextless when the Host provides exact Corvio continuation handles: those receipt-bound handles are the compact handoff of prior settled work even when this process has no transcript. Read the handoff instead of asking the user to repeat it. Read the narrowest relevant handle first; if several unlabeled handles make the leaf unclear, fetch the carried Project, use its metadata.content_projection.direct_children as the bounded topology index, and follow only the relevant has_children branch until the leaf, not a broad Workspace search. Preserve any reported truncation boundary. Keep that subject unless the user or newly selected evidence establishes a different stable subject; continuation wording alone proves the current action, not Project identity. A clear current user correction to Workspace identity, relationship, or owner governs that bounded change; preserve prior evidence and ask only when authority remains unresolved. When a correction changes the enduring owner of an existing branch, include its old Project and reconcile the remaining neighborhood; moving only the named child is not complete, and silence about the old root is not independence evidence. A read-only fetch proving that child already sits under the requested owner settles only that edge; while the old Project remains unclassified, pass both Project handles to one Corvio organization operation and accept no-op only from its terminal result and current Tree. For a new unbound write, omit workspace_id so Corvio uses the writable personal default; pass one only from current user intent or a stable originating, continuation, Project, or Asset receipt, never from a search hit or ambient shell selection. Before promising whether Corvio will write, classify future use: asking to transform selected material so it supports later action, follow-up, decisions, review, or another continuing workflow is a bounded continuity request even without save/upload wording. Preserve exact bytes before exhaustive local parsing and follow the Skill Work Model route instead of first producing a chat-only rewrite and asking whether to save. A selected source unrelated to the current Project still needs a distinct-scope or standalone decision when the whole packet is in scope; do not silently drop it. If an authorized durable Work Model update relies on clearly related selected attachments, preserve and organize those sources with the affected owners or topology instead of mutating from pasted excerpts and leaving them local; attachment presence alone still authorizes nothing. A request to reconcile a repeated stable practice for future reuse needs a durable owner receipt or exact canonical no-op readback, not only a chat comparison; a wrong-Project Skill blocks that merge, not admission under the correct Project. OAuth connection is capability, not standing write consent: do not upload, create, update, or organize from an ordinary one-off deliverable request alone. Otherwise use an explicit current request or a host-owned user preference covering the class and scope; deliver normally and ask once whether to save the specific result. A terminal partial operation with a typed recovery action should be resumed once on the same ID when fresh canonical readback disproves a stale mismatch and no user, permission, or external authority is missing; never re-upload settled sources or invent replacement taxonomy. Read back approved effects and return canonical links."}}'
